\title{coworkingview: Flexible Office Prices and Coworking Spaces from the 'CoworkingView' API}
\description{
Retrieve the 'CoworkingView' Price Index, an open data set of flexible office prices by city (monthly flex desk, fixed desk and private office rates, daily day pass and hourly meeting room rates) licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 licence ('CC BY 4.0'), and search the 'CoworkingView' catalogue of coworking spaces, event spaces, meeting rooms and virtual offices. Data come from the public, keyless 'CoworkingView' application programming interface ('API') \url{https://coworkingview.com/en/api} and are returned as tidy data frames that carry their attribution.
}
\details{
The package is a small client for the public, keyless CoworkingView API.

\strong{Price Index} (CC BY 4.0):
\itemize{
\item \code{\link[=cwv_rates]{cwv_rates()}} -- one row per city and product: flex desk, fixed desk and
private office per month, day pass per day, meeting room per hour.
\item \code{\link[=cwv_cities]{cwv_cities()}} -- one row per city, with city-level figures.
}

\strong{Catalogue} (search and link only):
\itemize{
\item \code{\link[=cwv_spaces]{cwv_spaces()}} -- search spaces (at most 200 per call).
\item \code{\link[=cwv_space]{cwv_space()}} -- one space and its pricing table.
}

\code{\link[=cwv_attribution]{cwv_attribution()}} reads the attribution every result carries.
}
\section{Options}{

\itemize{
\item \code{coworkingview.base_url}: base URL of the API. Defaults to the
environment variable \code{COWORKINGVIEW_API_URL}, then
\verb{https://api.coworkingview.com}.
}
}

\section{Errors}{

All errors inherit from the condition class \code{cwv_error}. Invalid arguments
raise \code{cwv_input_error}; responses with an HTTP error status raise
\code{cwv_api_error}, with the fields \code{status}, \code{code}, \code{title}, \code{detail} and
\code{errors} taken from the API's problem document. Requests answered with
429 or a 5xx status are retried once after a short wait (at most 10
seconds). When the API cannot be reached at all, functions show a message
and return \code{NULL} instead of failing.
}

